From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Lulejian <jlulejian@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:55:20 -0700
Subject: [Extensions] Fix UAF in PostMessageSupport::PostJavaScriptMessage

Before this change, `PostMessageSupport::PostJavaScriptMessage()`
acquired a `WeakPtr` to `this` after calling
`target_frame->GlobalProxy(isolate)`. When `target_frame` had not yet
initialized its main-world V8 context (e.g., an `<iframe>` with
`sandbox="allow-same-origin"`), `GlobalProxy()` lazily created the V8
context and installed `chrome.loadTimes` bindings. A page-defined
JavaScript setter on a child frame named `chrome` could run during
context creation and synchronously detach the `MimeHandlerView` frame,
destroying `PostMessageSupport` before `GlobalProxy()` returned and
causing a heap-use-after-free when calling `weak_factory_.GetWeakPtr()`.

After this change, `PostMessageSupport::PostJavaScriptMessage()` safely
returns early without accessing freed memory if `this` is destroyed
during lazy V8 context initialization inside `GlobalProxy()`.

Bug: 569674220
Change-Id: Ica5ac362fd0d267cd00a41850df43a4f5c98d2ab
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8600383
